  "prose": [
    {
      "title": "Basic example",
      "text": "Wrap a series of `<Button>`s in a `<ButtonGroup>`.",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Button toolbar",
      "text": "Combine sets of `<ButtonGroup>`s into a `<ButtonToolbar>` for more complex components.\n\nFeel free to mix input groups with button groups in your toolbars.\nSimilar to the example above, you’ll likely need some utilities though\nto space things properly.",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Sizing",
      "text": "Instead of applying button sizing props to every button in a group, just\nadd `size` prop to the `<ButtonGroup>`.",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Nesting",
      "text": "You can place other button types within the\n`<ButtonGroup>` like `<DropdownButton>`s.",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Vertical variation",
      "text": "Make a set of buttons appear vertically stacked rather than\nhorizontally, by adding `vertical` to the `<ButtonGroup>`.\n**Split button dropdowns are not supported here.**",
      "format": "md"
    }
  ],
